      <agendaitemid>5494</agendaitemid>
      <agendaitemtitle>Treasury Management Strategy, Annual Investment Strategy and Minimum Revenue Provision Policy Statement 2026/27</agendaitemtitle>
      <agendatext>&lt;div class="WordSection1"&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;This report outlines the
Council&amp;rsquo;s Prudential Indicators for 2026/27 &amp;ndash; 2028/29
and sets out the Treasury Strategy for this period. It fulfils
three key reports required by the Local Government Act
2003:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style=
"margin-left:24.0pt; text-indent:-18.0pt"&gt;&lt;span style=
""&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;1)&lt;span style=
"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span style=""&gt;reporting Prudential Indicators required by the
CIPFA Prudential Code for Capital Finance in Local
Authorities,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style=
"margin-left:24.0pt; text-indent:-18.0pt"&gt;&lt;span style=
""&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;2)&lt;span style=
"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span style=""&gt;a Treasury Management Strategy in accordance with
the CIPFA Code of Practice on Treasury Management,&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style=
"margin-left:24.0pt; text-indent:-18.0pt"&gt;&lt;span style=
""&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;3)&lt;span style=
"font:7.0pt &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;
&lt;span style=""&gt;an Investment Strategy in accordance with the
Ministry of Housing, Community and Local Government (MHCLG)
Investment Guidance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal"&gt;&lt;span style=""&gt;It also fulfils the statutory
duty to approve a Minimum Revenue Provision Policy (MRP) Statement
for 2026/27&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
</agendatext>
      <actualmeetingdate>19/02/2026</actualmeetingdate>
      <agendaitemnumber>5</agendaitemnumber>
      <agendaitemsubnumber>a)  </agendaitemsubnumber>
      <fulldisplaynumberformat>CL.059</fulldisplaynumberformat>
      <authorusername>Joseph Abbey</authorusername>
      <commentlabel1>Presented By</commentlabel1>
      <commenttext1>
      </commenttext1>
      <commentlabel2>Actions</commentlabel2>
      <commenttext2>
      </commenttext2>
      <minutesnonemptyhtmlbody>&lt;div class="WordSection1"&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;The Chair of the
Audit and Standards Committee, Councillor Hughes, introduced the
report and advised that a small amendment had been approved by the
Audit and Standards Committee which had not been reflected in the
published papers, this would be introduced as an amendment in
debate.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;Councillor Hughes
outlined that the report set out the Council&amp;rsquo;s treasury
management strategy, investment strategy, minimum revenue provision
and ethical investment policy, with no significant changes from
previous years. He referred to the updated capital spending plans
on page 21 table 3.1 and capital financing arrangements, including
the use of borrowing. He explained the approach to minimum revenue
provision for the General Fund and the earmarked reserve for the
Housing Revenue Account. He referred to the estimated future
balances set out at page 23, table 3.4, noting that while these
were estimates and likely to change, balances were expected to
reduce over time as reserves and capital receipts were used and
further borrowing undertaken.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;He highlighted the
forecast borrowing position, borrowing limits and the continued use
of internal borrowing. He outlined the annual investment strategy,
noting that the introduction of IFRS 9 for existing investments had
been deferred to April 2029 and that an earmarked investment risk
reserve was held to mitigate potential impacts. Councillor Hughes
also advised that the current ethical investment policy remained in
place pending completion of a revised policy currently under
review.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;Proposed by
Councillor Hughes and seconded by Councillor Kennedy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;Councillor Braun
proposed an amendment to include the changes Audit and Standards
Committee had agreed to, this included adding &amp;lsquo;subject to
further considerations being given to funding raised through
community climate based investments&amp;rsquo; after
&amp;lsquo;2026/27&amp;rsquo; in paragraph b) of the decision. Councillor
Pearcy seconded the amendment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;Councillors Hughes
and Kennedy accepted the proposal as a friendly amendment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;Councillor Luff
drew attention to the Council&amp;rsquo;s comparatively low level of
borrowing in relation to other councils and commented that this
reflected good financial management whilst still being able to
invest in local communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;Councillor Kennedy
described the Treasury Management report as an important
transparency tool which showed how the council managed its money,
debt and investments. The report demonstrated that capital spending
plans were affordable, prudent and sustainable and that the Council
had significant unused capacity to invest in capital expenditure in
an affordable and sustainable way. He noted that losses in the
Lothbury and Hermes property funds had been offset by an investment
risk reserve, and that there was no impact on wider Council
finances. He emphasised the importance of environmental, social and
governance considerations within the investment strategy, which was
currently under review.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;Councillor Hughes
thanked Maxine and Joseph for drafting the report and the rest of
the team for their hard work. He also highlighted the continued
good management of the Council and urged Members to support the
resolution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;On being put to the
vote, the Motion was carried with 40 votes in favour, 0 against and
3 abstentions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class="MsoNormal" style="text-align:justify"&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
